    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 48 tests run, 0 failures/errors, including the new `Cp35Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for owner creation. A new owner that isn't a hard duplicate (its identity key is unique) but shares an existing owner's `lastName` + `postcode` with a *different* telephone is still created and flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32). These generate the corresponding `OwnerDto` accessors, which MapStruct auto-maps by name.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) persistent fields with `@Column` mappings and getters/setters.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added `possible_duplicate` and `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the `owners` table.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 After the hard-duplicate (identity-key) check, it scans existing owners for one with the same normalized last name and equal postcode but a different telephone, picking the earliest by id. It sets `possibleDuplicate = true` / `possibleDuplicateOf = <that id>` when found, otherwise `false` / `null`.\n\nThe soft-match reuses the existing `normalizeForHousehold` helper for case-insensitive last-name comparison and only runs when a postcode is present, staying consistent with the surrounding rules.",
